CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*i)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct fc_internal)...)
#145: FILE: drivers/scsi/scsi_transport_fc.c:2233:
+	i = kzalloc(sizeof(struct fc_internal),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

